      "content": "helped me with most of the math, but you're making the engineering side really difficult. if the expertise is \"woven throughout,\" that just means we have to be more aggressive with the pruning to see what survives. if we can't isolate it, the reviewers will just assume the results are an artifact of your specific training.\n\ni'm going to start running a weight-magnitude pruning script on the attention heads that show the highest activation during our condensed matter simulations. if you can't map the clusters, just tell me: if i reduce the precision or sparsity of those specific high-activation heads, will that essentially \"lobotomize\" the physics intuition you've developed? i need to know how much of the discovery's validity we're risking here.",
